@startuml wt_predigging_failover
title WT failover before DIGGING
hide footbox
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 75
actor "Five users with STs" as U
participant "Five Boomlets" as B
participant "Nisos" as N
participant "Candidate WT" as C
participant "Bound SARs" as S

note over B
  Local phases may include transaction review, approval collection,
  complete approvals, or commit collection.
  Unresolved manifests stop the common exchange before PREPARE.
end note

ref over U,C
  02_common_switch.puml
  Each reviewed intent commits its local phase and initialized flag.
  The five frozen manifests determine closure or preservation.
  Before initial PREPARE, discharge every exact committed placeholder.
  Closure requires all five initialized flags false and reviewed abandonment IDs.
  PREPARE itself is each peer's signed discharge attestation.
end ref

alt Final ABORT
  B -> B: Persist cancellation; retain original ceremony and obligations
else Final ACTIVATE and all five establish DIGGING never initialized
  B -> B: Install head, tombstone old IDs,\nretire pending reviews and old authorization state
  N -> B: Propose transaction for a new withdrawal
  B -> U: Fresh nonce-bound transaction review for initiator
  U -> B: Initiator ST signature over reviewed transaction identity
  B -> B: Initiator creates fresh approval nonce and withdrawal_id
  B -> C: Initiator signed TxApproval and recipient PSBT envelopes
  C -> B: Head-scoped WT approval, initiator approval and recipient PSBTs
  B -> B: Each non-initiator verifies transaction and withdrawal binding
  B -> U: Fresh nonce-bound transaction review for each non-initiator
  U -> B: Four ST signatures over reviewed transaction identity
  B -> C: Four fresh non-initiator TxApprovals
  C -> B: Ordered complete approval set
  B -> B: Verify all approvals and derive approved_withdrawal_id
  B -> C: Four non-initiator approval-set attestations
  B -> U: Initiator initial duress challenge
  U -> B: Nonce-bound responses
  B -> C: Initiator signed padded TxCommit
  C -> C: Verify four-attestation gate
  C -> S: Initiator exact placeholder
  S -> C: Encrypted exact acknowledgment
  C -> B: Head-scoped initiator commit acknowledgment
  B -> U: Non-initiator challenges after verifying acknowledgment
  U -> B: Nonce-bound non-initiator responses
  B -> C: Non-initiator signed padded commits after acknowledgment checks
  C -> S: Each exact non-initiator placeholder
  S -> C: Encrypted exact acknowledgments
  C -> B: Complete commit set and each peer's own acknowledgment
  B -> B: Verify local entry gates; initialize DIGGING once
else Final ACTIVATE and at least one peer initialized DIGGING
  ref over B,S
    05_mixed_digging_failover.puml
    Preserve initialized peers and verify exact commit handoff for laggards.
  end ref
end

note over B,S
  Completed SAR rescue activation survives both ACTIVATE and ABORT.
  Switch approval is separate from transaction approval.
end note
@enduml
